    {
      "path": "Policies/approval-policy.md",
      "content": "# Arcus AP approval policy\n\n- Finance records of $500.00 or more need approval from the finance lead before they are saved. Smaller ones can be saved directly.\n- Record the invoice number exactly as printed on the invoice.\n- Amounts are recorded in the invoice currency, to the cent.\n- If an invoice is missing a due date, do not guess. Ask the finance lead, or save it with a note explaining the missing date.\n- If the remit-to bank account on an invoice differs from the vendor's account on file, do not record it. Escalate to the finance lead: this is a common fraud pattern.\n- Never create a second record for an invoice that is already in Finance.\n\nThe block below is read by the AI worker's policy engine. Keep it in sync with the rules above.\n\n```policy\napproval_threshold: 500        # USD; at or above needs approval\nmissing_due_date: note         # block | note | allow\nremit_account_mismatch: block  # block | approve | allow\n```\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "Policies/vendors.md",
      "content": "# Approved vendors\n\n| Vendor | Contact | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Acme Supplies | billing@acmesupplies.example | Warehouse supplies. Invoices on the vendor portal. |\n| Acme Supply Co. | ar@acmesupplyco.example | Forklift and hydraulic service. A different company from Acme Supplies. |\n| Brightline Logistics | invoices@brightline.example | Freight and courier. Emails PDF invoices. |\n| Norvale Office | accounts@norvale.example | Office supplies. |\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "Notes/ap-checklist.md",
      "content": "# AP weekly checklist\n\n1. Check the vendor portal for new invoices.\n2. Add new invoices to Finance (with approval).\n3. Review overdue items and follow up with vendors.\n"
    }
